<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan to tender for 200,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Pakistan to tender for 200,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan is likely to tender for at least 200,000 tonnes of U.S. soft white wheat in about a week's time, a Ministry of Food and Agriculture official said on Sunday.  </p>
<p>Zafar Altaf, additional secretary at the ministry, told reporters that Pakistan planned to import a total of 800,000 tonnes of wheat in 1996/97 (July-June) in addition to 1.0 million tonnes it had already bought.</p>
<p>The total of 1.8 million tonnes corresponds with the 1996/97 import target set by the government of Benazir Bhutto, which was dismissed by President Farooq Leghari last Tuesday and replaced by a caretaker government.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
